**User:**

I like those colors. How would I change the background and text colors in Drafter?

**Assistant:**

You can use Drafter's `add_website_css()` function to customize the appearance of your website.

First, change your website theme to `"none"` so the default theme doesn't override your custom colors:

```python
set_website_style("none")
```

Then use CSS to style the application:

```python
add_website_css("""
#drafter-body-- {
    background-color: #17251b !important;
    color: #eee8d5 !important;
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: auto;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
}
""")
```

**User:**

How do I make the headings tan and the buttons green?

**Assistant:**

You can add additional CSS rules to the same `add_website_css()` section.

For headings:

```css
#drafter-body-- h1,
#drafter-body-- h2,
#drafter-body-- h3 {
    color: #d6bd8a !important;
}
```

For buttons:

```css
#drafter-body-- button {
    background-color: #405b3c !important;
    color: white !important;
    border: 1px solid #75845c;
    border-radius: 7px;
    padding: 10px 16px;
    margin: 5px;
    font-weight: bold;
}
```

You can also add a hover effect:

```css
#drafter-body-- button:hover {
    background-color: #65764b !important;
}
```

**User:**

What about the text boxes and dropdown menus? I want those to match too.

**Assistant:**

You can style those using the input, textarea, and select CSS selectors:

```css
#drafter-body-- input,
#drafter-body-- textarea,
#drafter-body-- select {
    background-color: #eee8d5 !important;
    color: #263326 !important;
    border: 1px solid #9b895f;
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 9px;
}
```

This keeps the form fields light so the user can easily read what they type.

